{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmRXgM1cZKE7xf8swkCY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recorded TC-055 as a **pass**. The six-judge cross-family sitting holds up against the test's Method and Expected, and the page they judged is the dashboard as it stands at HEAD.\n\n**What I checked**, reproducing checks myself where I could rather than trusting the summary:\n- **Verdicts:** all six judges answered `APPROVE findings=0` and cited only the live anchors T2, T4, T5 and T8, never a retired one. Each verdict file matches the judge's own final message in its session log word for word, so none was edited afterwards.\n- **Judges:** six fresh `gpt-6-luna` sessions, a different model family from the dashboard's author. They ran with a read-only sandbox, made no tool calls, and saw no earlier verdict or author notes.\n- **Matrix:** the render run exited 0 with all 36 shots (3 widths × 2 themes × 5 tabs plus the landing fold). I confirmed the 328 tiles cover every shot exactly. I re-ran the attachment check: each judge received its full set of tiles, unchanged and in order.\n- **Inputs:** the rubric in every brief matches the rubric at HEAD. The intent rows and the scope lines of the six tests behind the live anchors are copied word for word from the registries, none cut short.\n- **Judged state:** HEAD differs from the rendered commit only by the earlier review file. `gen_trajectory.py --check` reports the dashboard up to date.\n\n**Things worth a follow-up** (none changes the result):\n- **Possible test gap for TC-305:** in the 1680px light How graph, two wires into CMP-006 run about 1px apart and their arrowheads overlap. They don't cross. The rubric routes a near-shared lane to TC-305, not to a verdict, so it's a candidate for that test's intake. My zoomed crops are in `review-tmp/adj991-crops/`.\n- **Shot set misses scrolled content:** at 1280 and 1680px, the When and How diagrams scroll sideways. Wiring past the scroll edge appears in no shot, so the judges saw only the visible part of those diagrams.\n- **Split by cell:** no single judge saw both themes. Combining a light and a dark judge per width still covers T5, since each theme only has to meet its own contrast bar.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `2cfe45f63` holds the record file (`docs/test/observations/TC-055.2026-11-06T090616Z.toml`, expires 2027-02-04). I left out the blank line after its subject, so the body runs into the subject when shown on one line. The trailers still parse, so I didn't amend it.\n- `fe0b19b20` holds the verdict `docs/reviews/wi-991/002-ADJUDICATE-4037ca4.md` (`OUTCOME: RECORDED result=pass`), ending with the `Loop-Session` and `WI: WI-991` trailers.\n\nThe commit hooks passed both times. I left the coordinator's `.requested` stub uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":121525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":811},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83c57a45-dae1-44ba-aec0-92b1d7d66e9f","uuid":"f40f6783-aa28-4adf-a48f-ac0498fbc1d2","timestamp":"2026-11-06T09:18:20.071Z","request_id":"req_011CgmRXg5szoAdNWCXmgzrU"}
